        "id": "ch2_2-1",
        "text": "What are cmdlets?\nCmdlets (pronounced command-lets ) are the commands we use in PowerShell. They can either be\nentered via a terminal application or through a script. They may be script-based and constructed\nfrom other cmdlets, or they may be binary cmdlets written in C# . The cmdlets that install by default\nwith PowerShell are binaries. Usually, cmdlets that we write ourselves or download from the internet\nwill be script-based. Cmdlets take an input object from the pipeline, perform an action on it, and\ngenerally return an object for further processing. We will describe this in detail in Chapter 3 , The\nPowerShell Pipeline \u2013 How to String Cmdlets Together .\nEsta secci\u00f3n contiene las siguientes subsecciones\n\u2022 Exploring cmdlet structure\n\u2022 The correct use of aliases\nSi deseas explorar cualquiera de estas subsecciones, puedes pregunt\u00e1rmelo directamente.",
